---
description: Every change ships as an open pull request, reviewed on GitHub
alwaysApply: true
---

Review happens on GitHub, not in chat. `AGENTS.md` has the full section; the
non-negotiable parts are:

- Every turn that changes code ends with a pushed branch and an open pull request. Do not
  wait for chat confirmation before opening it.
- Open the PR ready for review, never as a draft.
- Put the review context in the PR description - what changed, why, how it was verified -
  and assume the reviewer reads only GitHub.
- Close the turn by stating that the PR is open and waiting for review, with the link.
- When an implementation choice is ambiguous, decide it, ship it, and record the rejected
  alternative in the PR description instead of stopping to ask.
- If the PR tool reports that creation was only registered for approval, say so and name the
  branch; that gate is an account-level Cloud Agent setting, not something this repository
  controls.
